print(series.value_counts())    # ✅ Use value_counts() with parentheses
++++++++++++++++++some imp points+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Tuple/List → already a sequence of elements. Pandas can directly treat each element as a row in the Series.

String → is treated as one single object by pandas. If you pass "Hello World" directly, pandas will think it’s just one value.
That’s why we used list(a) to break it into characters first.

